---
/**
 * Select Component
 *
 * STATUS: KEPT AS REACT (src/components/ui/select.tsx)
 *
 * RATIONALE FOR KEEPING AS REACT:
 * This component uses @radix-ui/react-select which provides:
 * - Portal rendering for dropdown positioning (z-index layering)
 * - Complex keyboard navigation (Arrow keys, Home, End, PageUp, PageDown, Enter, Escape)
 * - Focus trap and focus management
 * - Scroll buttons for long lists
 * - ARIA attributes and full accessibility support
 * - Composable sub-components (Trigger, Content, Item, Value, Group, Separator, ScrollUpButton, ScrollDownButton)
 * - Animated open/close transitions
 *
 * Conversion Complexity Analysis:
 * - Estimated ~500-700 lines of vanilla JS/Alpine.js to replicate
 * - Extensive accessibility testing required
 * - Custom portal positioning implementation needed
 * - Focus trap logic to implement from scratch
 * - Not currently used in the codebase (grep confirmed no usage)
 *
 * Decision: Keep as React component with @astrojs/react integration
 * Use with `client:load` directive when needed in Astro pages
 *
 * USAGE IN ASTRO PAGES:
 * ```astro
 * ---
 * import { Select, SelectTrigger, SelectValue, SelectContent, SelectItem } from '@/components/ui/select';
 * ---
 *
 * <Select client:load defaultValue="option1">
 *   <SelectTrigger>
 *     <SelectValue placeholder="Select an option" />
 *   </SelectTrigger>
 *   <SelectContent>
 *     <SelectItem value="option1">Option 1</SelectItem>
 *     <SelectItem value="option2">Option 2</SelectItem>
 *   </SelectContent>
 * </Select>
 * ```
 *
 * Alternative: Use native HTML <select> for simpler cases:
 * ```astro
 * <select class="...">
 *   <option value="1">Option 1</option>
 *   <option value="2">Option 2</option>
 * </select>
 * ```
 */
---

<div class="select-usage-docs">
  <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
    The Select component is kept as React. See component documentation for usage.
  </p>
</div>
